    · tests_a2_withdrawal_gate: that the LIVE key actually has withdrawals disabled — it proves the GATE reads the right host and refuses a permissive key. The key's real settings are a fact about the account, established by arm() at run time and by the operator's own out-of-band check, never by this suite
    · tests_alarm_redelivery: that a resent page is READ. It proves the queue drains and never double-sends; whether an operator sees a [补发] arriving hours late is outside any test. Nor does it cover a Telegram that accepts and silently drops — delivered_offbox means the API said yes, not that a human saw it
